(ned RACK CALIBRATION -- P1..Pn fork centres by probing the energized)
(holders with the empty spindle. Operator spec 2026-08-04: start with the)
(spindle CENTERED 10 mm above the P1 holder top - THAT pose is the datum.)
(  #1 = fork count, 0 -> 14        #2 = Y step to the next fork, 0 -> 92)
(Step default 92.0 = the jig pitch. The first run used 45 from a misread)
(spec and landed between forks; every move is a probe, so it aborted clean.)
(Requires: EMPTY spindle, holders energized onto the toolsetter input,)
(machine homed, started AT the P1 datum pose.)
o<rack_cal> sub
  #<n>    = #1
  #<step> = #2
  o5 if [#<n> LE 0]
    (default = the live fork count in #3973, not a literal)
    #<n> = #3973
    o99 if [#<n> LT 1]
      #<n> = 14
    o99 endif
  o5 endif
  o6 if [#<step> LE 0]
    #<step> = 92.0
  o6 endif
  o7 if [#<_metric> EQ 0]
    (abort, RACK CAL: switch to MM first)
  o7 endif
  (the datum pose IS work zero: the operator zeroes X Y Z centred 10 mm)
  (above the P1 top, THEN starts. Anything else is a dirty reference and)
  (the cycle refuses rather than probing from an unknown frame.)
  o9 if [[ABS[#<_x>] GT 0.001] OR [ABS[#<_y>] GT 0.001] OR [ABS[#<_z>] GT 0.001]]
    (abort, RACK CAL: work XYZ is not zero here - zero all three at the datum pose first, centred 10 mm above P1 - NOT starting)
  o9 endif

  #3071 = 0

  (datum = wherever the operator parked us: centred, 10 mm above the top)
  #<_rc_cx>   = #<_x>
  #<_rc_cy>   = #<_y>
  #<_rc_safe> = #<_z>
  (Fit verify -70: at -75 the stud was reaching the drawbar inside the bore)
  (and tripping the verify - operator 2026-08-04.)
  (FIND LEVEL: 20 mm below the parked pose for the FIRST fork, then each)
  (fork hands the next one its own measured top - 10, in rc_locate. This)
  (replaced a fixed -50 descent - operator 2026-08-16: centring that far)
  (down is counterproductive.)
  #<_rc_pfind> = [#<_z> - 20.0]
  (VERIFY DEPTH 60, operator 2026-08-16: at 70 it was reaching the)
  (drawbar inside the spindle bore, not the taper. Same failure mode)
  (as the 75 -> 70 change on 2026-08-04, one step further out.)
  (This is also the bottom end of the fast-probe ramp, so the ramp)
  (now spans 20..60 rather than 20..70 and reaches #3005 at 60.)
  #<_rc_p60>  = [#<_z> - 60.0]
  (REACH FOLLOWS THE FIND LEVEL. 8.0 was sized for the old -50)
  (descent. The find now happens at -20, 30 mm higher, and the)
  (spindle taper is ISO-30 -- 7:24 per docs/components.md -- so its)
  (radius shrinks 0.14583 mm per mm of Z: 30 * 3.5/24 = 4.375 mm)
  (more bore-to-taper gap on every side. The 8.0 probe ran out of)
  (travel before the taper and G38.2 raised its own no-contact)
  (error, which fires before rc_touch's guard can say anything.)
  (12.4 is the geometric floor; 14.0 was still short on the iron,)
  (so the operator called 18.0 on 2026-08-16. A longer reach costs)
  (nothing when the taper is there -- contact stops the probe.)
  #<_rc_reach> = 18.0
  #<_rc_ftr>  = #3006
  #<_rc_fpr>  = #3004
  (_rc_fpr0 is the UNSCALED fast probe and _rc_ptop the Z at which it)
  (is used in full. rc_locate overwrites _rc_fpr per find level, so the)
  (original has to survive somewhere or every fork after the first)
  (would inherit the previous fork's reduced feed.)
  #<_rc_fpr0> = #3004
  #<_rc_ptop> = [#<_z> - 20.0]
  #<_rc_fla>  = #3005
  #<_rc_fck>  = #3004
  o8 if [[#<_rc_ftr> LE 0] OR [#<_rc_fpr> LE 0] OR [#<_rc_fla> LE 0]]
    (abort, RACK CAL: probe feeds 3004-3006 are not set - set them on the probe screen first)
  o8 endif

  #<i> = 1
  o10 while [#<i> LE #<n>]
    (RESUME: a fork with data is SKIPPED, its stored centre reused for the)
    (prediction chain -- an aborted run keeps everything already located and)
    (a restart from the datum only probes the holders without data)
    (complete = flag set AND a real Z. Old runs stored XY with no Z --)
    (those count INCOMPLETE and get fully remeasured, which is also how)
    ("start over" works: any fork without all three is remeasured on START)
    #<base> = [4100 + [#<i> * 4]]
    o13 if [[#[#<base> + 3] EQ 1] AND [ABS[#[#<base> + 2]] GT 0.001]]
      #<offx> = [#<_abs_x> - #<_x>]
      #<offy> = [#<_abs_y> - #<_y>]
      #<offz> = [#<_abs_z> - #<_z>]
      #<_rc_cx> = [#[#<base>] - #<offx>]
      #<_rc_cy> = [#[#<base> + 1] - #<offy>]
      (a SKIPPED fork still owns the find level for the next one, or the)
      (chain would carry a level measured two or more forks back)
      #<_rc_pfind> = [[#[#<base> + 2] - #<offz>] - 10.0]
      (PRINT, RACK CAL fork #<i>: already located - skipped)
    o13 else
      o<rc_locate> call [#<i>]
    o13 endif
    
    (next fork: predicted from the centre just FOUND, one step over in Y-)
    #<_rc_cy> = [#<_rc_cy> - #<step>]
    #<i> = [#<i> + 1]
  o10 endwhile

  G90
  G1 Z[#<_rc_safe>] F[#<_rc_ftr>]

  #3071 = 1
  (PRINT, RACK CAL DONE: #<n> forks located and stored in the 4100 block)
  (DEBUG, RACK CAL done: #<n> forks located - see the log for each centre)
o<rack_cal> endsub
M2
